{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>I.</b> I alone — He is <b>YHWH</b>, who grants existence, the First Being, who is known to you through tradition and through sign." "<b>Your Elohim.</b> And I fulfill what you accepted upon yourself — that I be your Elohim, without intermediary. Therefore to Me alone shall you pray and Me shall you serve, without any intermediary." "<b>Who brought you out of the land of Egypt.</b> Through acts contrary to the workings of every intermediary that is nature and the celestial order — and this, as you received when you said: זֶה אֵלִי וְאַנְוֵהוּ וגו׳ (Exodus 15:2)." "<b>From the house of slaves.</b> To remove all coercion, for where coercion is present there is no place for any commandment in its proper form."], :book :exodus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:26:25.886967557Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}